From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: the shader set's compute records are prepared and a dispatch takes a prepared one (EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_COMPUTE=1), off by default

Switch: EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_COMPUTE=1 (the switch of 0780; needs 0780). Off: nothing changes (the
preparation reads no compute record, a dispatch translates as before).

Why: with 0780 the set holds the recipe's compute records, but the preparation and the store
were graphics only, and a compute pipeline asked in play was always translated on the GPU thread
(94 in the d4 start).

What, with the switch:
- PrepareShaderSet gives ReadRecords an on_compute callback. A compute record is prepared like a
  graphics one: its key's store hash is KeptComputeHash (the key hash with "compute1" mixed in,
  so it never meets a graphics key's), known or struck-out records are skipped, it waits its turn
  exactly as a graphics record does: 0770's gate (cap, the before-play pass's time limit and skip
  flag, index commit, memory floor with the before-play pass's wait counted over the whole pass
  (0772), disk floor and its warning, yield to the runtime's builds, duty cycle, one slot) is
  moved unchanged into a lambda, `admit(hash, hand_back)`, that both kinds call; then a worker of
  the pass's own pool (0770's threads before play, the pipeline workers beside the game)
  translates it and builds it once with the driver's own cache only, and keeps its SPIR-V, its
  info and the answers its translation got in the prepared store (FlagPredicted |
  FlagShaderSet), or remembers it as not keepable. Before play the compute jobs add to the
  pass's kept and failed counts; the list pass (graphics keys only here) skips compute records.
- CreateComputePipeline (the pools one) takes an optional Stages* that receives the SPIR-V and
  the info (stage 0) before the IR may be freed; with it, the null pointer slot table is not
  touched and the driver-only cache is used.
- On the GPU thread, a compute pipeline that is not in compute_cache first tries
  CreateKeptComputePipeline: found in the store under KeptComputeHash, its answers are checked
  against the live dispatch with FileEnvironment::AnswersHoldFor (handle words listed from the
  kept info as CreateKeptGraphicsPipeline lists them; shared memory and workgroup are checked
  there too), then the pipeline is made from the kept SPIR-V and info (built on a worker as a
  translated one). Anything that does not hold, cannot be read or throws gives null and the
  dispatch translates as before; a refused key is not tried again this session. Not for a
  rebuild (EDEN_UP_NULL_POINTER_SLOTS): that one is made from the live state on purpose. The
  rest of the path is unchanged: the record still goes to vulkan.bin, the first-start list and
  the pointer slot bookkeeping as before.
- One line every 10 s while it is used: "Kept compute translations in the last 10 s: N compute
  pipelines made without translating, M refused (reasons)", and one line per preparation pass
  with the number of compute records read.

Not done here: the live-first pass (prep_shader_set.live) only learns of vertex and pixel
programs, so compute records are prepared in the whole-file pass, in the file's order. 0784 puts
the C rows of the list files first (by KeptComputeHash) and counts compute keys in the before-play
pass's done / total; 0785 keeps them off the per-start cap.

T161s: made again on top of 0770-0772 (T157). The T158 version moved the T151 gate into `admit`;
this one moves 0770's gate (with 0772's whole-pass memory wait) instead, and the compute callback
queues on 0770's job_workers. Needs 0770 and 0772.
